  "title": "RBI introduces one-time approval route for MFs, insurers, pension funds to acquire bank shares",
  "summary": "Under the earlier framework, investors whose aggregate shareholding in a bank fell below 5 per cent had to seek RBI approval again before making a subsequent acquisition of major shareholding. RBI has now introduced a one-time approval route for mutual funds, insurance companies and pension funds for subsequent acquisitions of major shareholding, up to 10 per cent of a bank's paid-up share capital or voting rights on an aggregate basis, these directions take effect immediately from October 1, 2026.",
